406 - Love Consecrates the Humblest Act
 / 
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 406
Topic: Doctrines - 

Verse 1:
[D]Love [G]consecrates the humblest act
[G]And haloes [D]mercy's [C/E]deeds;
[G]It [C]sheds a [G]benediction [D]sweet
[G]And hallows human needs.

Verse 2:
[D]When [G]in the shadow of the cross
[G]Christ knelt [D7/A]and [D]washed [C/E]the feet
[G]Of [C]His disciples, [D]He [C]gave [D]us
[G]A sign of love complete.

Verse 3:
[D]Love [G]serves and [C/G]willing, [G]stoops to serve;
[G]What Christ [D7/A]in [D]love [C/E]so true
[G]Has [C]freely [G]done [D]for one [C]and [D]all,
[G]Let us now gladly do!
